PROVENANCE AND CREDITS

WordBuddy began life as WorkBuddy, which had its origins as StudyBuddy, which was written from scratch using two open-source projects as reference and inspiration (ideas and architecture, not code):

  - pluely (https://github.com/iamsrikanthnani/pluely), GPL-3.0 — the
    floating-bar desktop-assistant concept and Tauri architecture
    approach. A file-level provenance audit on 2026-07-03 (recorded in
    docs/DECISIONS.md, ADR-041) found no copied code: line-level overlap
    between the two codebases is 1-9% per candidate file and consists of
    Tauri boilerplate and standard API calls. Command names and tuning
    parameters were borrowed; expression was not.

  - Clicky (https://github.com/farzaa/clicky) — inspiration for the
    spring-physics cursor pointing overlay and idle-triggered tutoring
    concepts. Implemented independently.

The AGPL-3.0-licensed OmniParser/Ultralytics YOLOv8 model that earlier
versions of StudyBuddy could optionally download was removed from this
codebase on 2026-07-03 (ADR-041). No AGPL or GPL code or models remain.

Third-party dependencies (Rust crates and npm packages) remain under
their own permissive licenses (MIT/Apache-2.0) as declared in their
respective manifests.

